    <title>Can LLM Judges Be Trusted? Measuring Agreement
  with Human Raters Across Tasks</title>
    <summary>  Large language models are increasingly used as automatic judges of
generated text. We measure agreement between LLM judges and human raters
on four tasks and find that agreement depends strongly on the task.
</summary>
