    <title>Self-Preference in LLM-as-a-Judge: When Models Favor
  Their Own Family ($\alpha$-Calibrated Scoring)</title>
    <summary>  Judges rate outputs from their own model family more highly. We
quantify this effect with an $\alpha$-calibrated score across six model
families.
</summary>
    <author>
      <name>Farah Mock</name>
    </author>
